  {
    "id": "c093",
    "name": "23.C Statement of student rights",
    "text": "C. Chairperson gives statement of the student’s rights to fairness under this process: 1. To bring one adviser of the accused/accuser’s choice from the University community to provide passive assistance during the hearing (the adviser may not serve as a witness) 2. To present witnesses on their own behalf 3. To question witnesses appearing against them 4. To submit verbal arguments 5. To remain silent and not testify against themselves. The accused/accuser should remember that if they remain silent, the Board is compelled to hear the case and render a decision based upon the evidence presented."
